00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.460
Joe: Individuals with autism
typically struggle with fully

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.869
engaging in conversations.

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.330
They may interrupt the person
talking or decide the conversation

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.080
is over and walk away while the
other person is still speaking.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.580
They can suffer from Social imagination
difficulties by not having the

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.829
ability to imagine what another
person may be feeling, thinking

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.550
or experiencing and therefore lack
the ability to relate to others.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.569
They may have trouble with eye contact
which is important for communicating

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.580
interest in having a social interaction
with someone, and this difficulty

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.830
can often be misconstrued by others
as disinterest or inattention.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.070
To individuals with autism social
interactions can appear unnatural and very

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.570
stressful so many may try to avoid them.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.940
They suffer from social inhibition,
consciously or subconsciously

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.929
avoiding social interaction
because of the possibility of

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:51.670
disapproving reactions from others.

00:00:52.799 --> 00:00:56.680
It can be difficult for individuals
with autism to make or keep friends and

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.430
they may say they don't need or want
friends and isolate themselves socially.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.940
They may have less interest in social
interaction for its own sake and be

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.460
more interested in things than in
people, and are often content when left

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.539
alone to pursue their own interests

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.080
Some choose to be social, however
their issues in social understanding

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:18.690
and empathy can prevent them from
smoothly engaging with others.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:22.740
An individual may know they are supposed
to use words to start a conversation

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.900
with others however, they may not
know quite how to use them, and may

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.110
end up having life-long difficulty
navigating through social situations.

